            "text_KwEnHH": {
              "type": "text",
              "settings": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Everyday steps.</strong> Many women get real relief from simple changes:</p>",
                "text_style": "body",
                "alignment": "left",
                "text_color": "",
                "custom_font_size": false,
                "font_size": 16,
                "font_size_mobile": 15,
                "custom_line_height": false,
                "line_height": 26,
                "line_height_mobile": 24,
                "custom_spacing": true,
                "margin_top": 0,
                "margin_bottom": 0,
                "margin_left": 0,
                "margin_right": 0
              },
              "blocks": {}
            },
            "text_NGe8XV": {
              "type": "text",
              "settings": {
                "text": "<ul><li>Dress in layers you can shed quickly, and keep the bedroom cool at night.</li><li>Notice your triggers. Spicy food, alcohol, caffeine and stress are common ones; a short symptom log makes patterns obvious.</li><li>Try slow, paced breathing at the first sign of a flash. Some studies find it reduces how bothersome flashes feel.</li></ul>",
                "text_style": "body",
                "alignment": "left",
                "text_color": "",
                "custom_font_size": false,
                "font_size": 16,
                "font_size_mobile": 15,
                "custom_line_height": true,
                "line_height": 36,
                "line_height_mobile": 24,
                "custom_spacing": true,
                "margin_top": 0,
                "margin_bottom": 0,
                "margin_left": 0,
                "margin_right": 0
              },
              "blocks": {}
            },
            "text_mAtczE": {
              "type": "text",
              "settings": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Products that may help.</strong> Some women find hormone-free supplements helpful, though the evidence is mixed and quality varies. We stock a small selection chosen for manufacturing quality, and we show the evidence level on every product page. Supplements are not FDA-approved to treat any condition, and what works for one woman may do nothing for another.</p>",
                "text_style": "body",
                "alignment": "left",
                "text_color": "",
                "custom_font_size": false,
                "font_size": 16,
                "font_size_mobile": 15,
                "custom_line_height": false,
                "line_height": 26,
                "line_height_mobile": 24,
                "custom_spacing": true,
                "margin_top": 0,
                "margin_bottom": 20,
                "margin_left": 0,
                "margin_right": 0
              },
              "blocks": {}
            },
            "text_wejyc7": {
              "type": "text",
              "settings": {
                "text": "<p><strong>When to see a clinician.</strong> If hot flashes are disrupting your sleep or your days, it is worth talking to a menopause-informed clinician. Effective treatments exist, including prescription options, and a clinician can help weigh benefits and risks for your situation. Bacton does not prescribe; we can help you prepare for that conversation.</p>",
                "text_style": "body",
                "alignment": "left",
                "text_color": "",
                "custom_font_size": false,
                "font_size": 16,
                "font_size_mobile": 15,
